ask(1544,'eliza','The screenshot transforms “I hate cats” into a response referring to “you hate cats.” What operation is illustrated?', ['Reusing captured text with a speaker-pronoun substitution','Measuring whether cats are actually present in a camera image','Retraining a sentiment model after the single sentence','Replacing every noun by the bot’s name'],['The response reframes the user’s words using the other conversational person.','The text example supplies no visual observation.','The displayed transformation does not establish model training.','Cats remains the content referent.'],kind='diagram',cites=[(1544,'figure','ELIZA dialogue screenshot, I hate cats exchange')])
ask(1544,'eliza','How should the slide’s claim that ELIZA has no memory beyond the previous statement be qualified using its original paper?', ['ELIZA had a limited mechanism storing transformed text for later use, not unrestricted semantic memory','ELIZA had no stored state of any kind, so the original MEMORY mechanism is only a printed response word','ELIZA’s stored transformed text proves it learned a complete world model during conversation','A limited memory mechanism and scripted responses are mutually exclusive designs'],['The original mechanism retained transformed material under bounded rules.','The paper describes an actual stored-text mechanism.','Limited state does not imply a learned world model.','The original implementation combines scripts and stored material.'],conflict=MEM)
ask(1545,'eliza-pipeline','Which sequence follows the six central boxes of the simplified ELIZA working diagram?', ['Tokenization → standardization → keyword extraction → decomposition → reassembly → post-processing','Tokenization → keyword extraction → reassembly → standardization → decomposition → post-processing','Standardization → reassembly → tokenization → keyword extraction → post-processing → decomposition','Keyword extraction → post-processing → tokenization → decomposition → standardization → reassembly'],['This is the stated flow through the diagram.','It assembles a reply before decomposing the input and changes the shown order.','The middle operations are out of the depicted order.','Post-processing is incorrectly moved before the main input analysis.'],kind='sequence',cites=[(1545,'figure','Six central labeled boxes and connecting arrows')])
