ask(1545,'eliza-pipeline','A supplied simplified script gives keyword sorry priority over I am by file order. The input contains both. Which conclusion is warranted?', ['Trace sorry first under this stipulated policy, without claiming that original ELIZA lacked explicit ranks','Trace I am first because every ELIZA implementation must prefer the longest keyword','Choose whichever word occurs last in the input regardless of the supplied script policy','Infer that the system must learn the priority from these two words at runtime'],['The stated policy determines this toy trace; the historical algorithm supports rank metadata.','No longest-match rule is stipulated here.','That is not the supplied priority rule.','The priority is programmed, not learned in this scenario.'],kind='algorithm_trace',ass=['Both keyword patterns match; the toy script explicitly uses file order.'],steps=['Find both matching keywords.','Apply the stipulated file-order priority.','Choose sorry for this trace; do not generalize that policy to every original script.'],conflict=RANK)
